Description: CVE-2026-84384 - bound zlib metadata decompression output (decompression bomb)
 libheif's "deflate"-encoded metadata path (mime/Exif/XMP items) is decompressed
 by metadata_compression.cc::inflate(), which repeatedly appends 8 KiB zlib
 output chunks to an unbounded std::vector with no accounting of the total
 decompressed size. A small crafted HEIF file can therefore expand a few KB of
 compressed metadata into gigabytes of output, exhausting memory and terminating
 the process (CWE-409, data amplification / decompression-bomb DoS).
 .
 The upstream fix (commit 21893e8f66c8b79363ca2809391b07d35e1a95ec, v1.23.2)
 bounds the decompression output using the heif_security_limits API and the
 brotli decoder, neither of which exists in the 1.15.1 codebase shipped by
 Debian bookworm (brotli support and heif_security_limits were introduced in
 v1.19.0). This is therefore a re-derived, target-native fix: it adds an
 explicit fixed cap on the accumulated decompressed output inside the older,
 zlib-only inflate() loop, aborting decompression (returning an empty buffer,
 the function's existing error convention) once the output exceeds a generous
 50 MiB limit. Legitimate compressed metadata items are far smaller, so no
 valid file is rejected. The brotli decompression vector from the upstream
 advisory does not exist in 1.15.1 and needs no corresponding change.
Origin: other, re-derived from upstream https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/commit/21893e8f66c8b79363ca2809391b07d35e1a95ec
Bug: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-24wx-9w62-c96w
Author: Patch Platoon AI <security@example.com>
Last-Update: 2026-09-20
--- a/libheif/metadata_compression.cc
+++ b/libheif/metadata_compression.cc
@@ -87,6 +87,15 @@ std::vector<uint8_t> inflate(const std::vector<uint8_t>& compressed_input)
   const int outBufferSize = 8192;
   uint8_t dst[outBufferSize];

+  // Bound the total decompressed output size to defend against a zlib
+  // "decompression bomb": a small crafted "deflate"-encoded metadata item can
+  // otherwise expand into gigabytes of output, exhausting memory and
+  // terminating the process (CWE-409 data amplification, CVE-2026-84384 /
+  // GHSA-24wx-9w62-c96w). Compressed metadata items (Exif/XMP/mime) are small
+  // in practice, so a generous fixed cap closes the amplification vector
+  // without rejecting any legitimate file.
+  const size_t maxDecompressedSize = 50 * 1024 * 1024; // 50 MiB
+
   z_stream strm;
   memset(&strm, 0, sizeof(z_stream));

@@ -126,6 +135,13 @@ std::vector<uint8_t> inflate(const std::vector<uint8_t>& compressed_input)
     // append decoded data to output

     output.insert(output.end(), dst, dst + outBufferSize - strm.avail_out);
+
+    // Enforce the decompression-bomb limit on the accumulated output.
+    if (output.size() > maxDecompressedSize) {
+      inflateEnd(&strm);
+      // TODO: return error
+      return {};
+    }
   } while (err != Z_STREAM_END);


