+**CVE-2026-62292 is a false positive for Debian 12 (Bookworm).** The vulnerable uncompressed `unci` tile-slicing path was introduced in libheif 1.16.0 and the advisory's affected range begins at 1.19.0, while Debian Bookworm ships 1.15.1. Since the vulnerable code does not exist in the deployed source tree, the package should be classified as **not affected** with the justification **`vulnerable_code_not_present`**.
+
+## CVE-2026-84444 — False Positive for Debian 12 (Bookworm)
+
+| Field                 | Value                                                                                                                 |
+| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| **CVE ID**            | CVE-2026-84444                                                                                                        |
+| **Component**         | libheif                                                                                                               |
+| **CWE**               | CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write                                                                                          |
+| **Distribution**      | Debian 12 (Bookworm)                                                                                                  |
+| **Bookworm package**  | `libheif` source package, version `1.15.1-1` / `1.15.1-1+deb12u1` (security/point-release respins on the 1.15.1 base) |
+| **Upstream affected** | libheif versions that ship the uncompressed (`unci`) tiled encoder (`WITH_UNCOMPRESSED_CODEC`)                         |
+| **Upstream fixed in** | libheif 1.23.2 (commit `e65071f59a1ac08aa1eb0d07a831deaf6bb4d03b`)                                                    |
+| **Assessment**        | **FALSE POSITIVE for Bookworm — package is not vulnerable, no patch required.**                                       |
+
+---
+
+### 1. Why this CVE is being flagged
+
+Scanners and the Debian security tracker match this CVE against older `libheif`
+versions because the advisory is treated as an upper-bound version comparison.
+Bookworm `1.15.1-1+deb12u1` is numerically below 1.23.2, so it is flagged.
+
+**Version comparison alone is incorrect here.** CVE-2026-84444 is a heap
+out-of-bounds write in the uncompressed (`unci`) tiled-image encoder, reachable
+via `heif_context_add_image_tile()` when `WITH_UNCOMPRESSED_CODEC` is enabled.
+That encoder lives under `libheif/codecs/uncompressed/*` and
+`libheif/image-items/unc_image.cc`. Those paths — and the uncompressed codec
+feature itself — were introduced upstream around **v1.18/v1.19** (~2023-04),
+after **v1.15.1** (2023-02-16).
+
+### 2. Why Bookworm's libheif 1.15.1 is not vulnerable
+
+The upstream fix (`e65071f5`) validates tile images against the frozen unci
+encoder configuration before `encode_tile()`. In libheif 1.15.1:
+
+- There is no `libheif/codecs/` or `libheif/image-items/` directory
+- There is no `unc_image.cc`, `encode_tile()`, or `WITH_UNCOMPRESSED_CODEC`
+- `heif_context_add_image_tile()` is not the unci tiled-encoder entry point
+
+There is no vulnerable (pre-fix) code to patch and no directory structure to
+map the fix onto (patch job result: `TARGET_MISMATCH`).
+
+### 3. Verification against upstream 1.15.1 (matches Bookworm)
+
+```bash
+ls libheif/codecs/uncompressed/ libheif/image-items/unc_image.cc   # missing
+grep -rn "WITH_UNCOMPRESSED_CODEC\|encode_tile\|add_unci" libheif/  # empty
+```
+
+Confirmed by the automated patcher against Debian bookworm
+`libheif` `1.15.1-1+deb12u1` (Jira TP-162519).
+
+### 4. VEX / scanner guidance
+
+```json
+{
+  "vulnerability": "CVE-2026-84444",
+  "products": [
+    "pkg:deb/debian/libheif@1.15.1-1+deb12u1?distro=bookworm"
+  ],
+  "status": "not_affected",
+  "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present"
+}
+```
+
+### 5. References
+
+* Advisory: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-j264-xvrp-5v7q
+* Upstream fix commit: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/commit/e65071f59a1ac08aa1eb0d07a831deaf6bb4d03b
+* Jira: https://slim-ai.atlassian.net/browse/TP-162519
+* Debian Bookworm libheif package: https://packages.debian.org/bookworm/libheif1
+
+### Conclusion
+
+**CVE-2026-84444 is a false positive for Debian 12 (Bookworm).** The vulnerable uncompressed (`unci`) tiled-image encoder was introduced around libheif 1.18/1.19, while Debian Bookworm ships 1.15.1. Since the vulnerable code does not exist in the deployed source tree, the package should be classified as **not affected** with the justification **`vulnerable_code_not_present`**.
