+### 1. Why this CVE is being flagged
+
+The advisory range is `<= 1.23.1` patched in 1.23.2 ([GHSA-xw34-mjcp-jqh8](https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-xw34-mjcp-jqh8)).
+Bookworm `1.15.1-1+deb12u1` is numerically below 1.23.2, so scanners flag it.
+
+**Version comparison alone is incorrect here.** CVE-2026-84446 is a sequence
+timing-table DoS: edit-list repeat plus an inflated movie-header duration
+amplifies one physical sample into a huge logical output count, so a 32-bit
+decode loop never terminates. All of that lives in `libheif/sequences/`
+(`track.cc`, `seq_boxes.cc`, `chunk.cc`) and `libheif/api/libheif/heif_sequences.cc`.
+
+### 2. Why Bookworm's libheif 1.15.1 is not vulnerable
+
+The sequences API first shipped in **libheif 1.20.0** (2025-07-01). Bookworm's
+orig tarball is **1.15.1** (2023-02-16), a flat `libheif/` tree with only
+`plugins/` as a subdirectory. Verified against `libheif_1.15.1.orig.tar.gz` and
+Debian `1.15.1-1+deb12u1` (series: CVE-2024-41311, CVE-2023-49462, CVE-2023-29659):
+
+- no `libheif/sequences/` directory
+- no `heif_sequences.cc` / `heif_sequences.h`
+- no `init_sample_timing_table`, `m_num_output_samples`,
+  `interpret_heif_file_sequences`, `heif_track_get_next_raw_sequence_sample`,
+  `Box_stts`, `Box_mvhd`, or `elst` symbols
+
+The upstream fix (`3a7a69ae`) cannot apply: every hunk targets files that do
+not exist. A crafted HEIF sequence file cannot reach the vulnerable loop.
+
+### 3. Verification
+
+```bash
+ls libheif/sequences libheif/api/libheif/heif_sequences.cc   # missing
+grep -rn "init_sample_timing_table\|m_num_output_samples\|heif_sequences" libheif/  # empty
+```
+
+Confirmed on Debian orig `libheif_1.15.1.orig.tar.gz` and
+`libheif_1.15.1-1+deb12u1.debian.tar.xz` (Jira TP-162520).
+
+### 4. VEX / scanner guidance
+
+```json
+{
+  "vulnerability": "CVE-2026-84446",
+  "products": [
+    "pkg:deb/debian/libheif@1.15.1-1+deb12u1?distro=bookworm"
+  ],
+  "status": "not_affected",
+  "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present"
+}
+```
+
+### 5. References
+
+* Advisory: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/security/advisories/GHSA-xw34-mjcp-jqh8
+* Upstream fix commit: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/commit/3a7a69ae325f652e48c026b8241ab25bedf44d9b
+* Sequences API introduced: https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/releases/tag/v1.20.0
+* Jira: https://slim-ai.atlassian.net/browse/TP-162520
+* Debian Bookworm libheif package: https://packages.debian.org/bookworm/libheif1
+
+### Conclusion
+
+**CVE-2026-84446 is a false positive for Debian 12 (Bookworm).** The vulnerable HEIF image-sequence / track timing path was introduced in libheif 1.20.0, while Debian Bookworm ships 1.15.1. Since the vulnerable code does not exist in the deployed source tree, the package should be classified as **not affected** with the justification **`vulnerable_code_not_present`**.
